REPORTED upstream 2026-08-27:
https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/issues/29664

Note the repo moved: containers/podman -> podman-container-tools/podman.
The old path still redirects for browsing but the GitHub search API does not
resolve it, which is worth knowing for future lookups.

Verified before filing, because "retest on a current release" would have been
the first reply otherwise:

  Podman 5.4.2 (Debian 13's package, the systemd socket)  ZERSTOERT
  Podman 5.8.4 (~/.local/bin, current upstream)           ZERSTOERT

Both: before attach `exited/exit=4`, wait `{"StatusCode":4}`; after attach
`created/exit=0`, wait `{"StatusCode":-1}`.

Worth knowing about this machine, and the reason the version question came up
at all: there are two podman installations. The systemd user socket starts
/usr/bin/podman (5.4.2, Debian package) while ~/.local/bin/podman is 5.8.4 and
is what the CLI resolves to. Every measurement in this distribution's POD and
Changes names 5.4.2 and is correctly labelled -- but it is the older of the two,
and any future measurement should say which socket it used.

No duplicate found upstream. The closest existing issues are #8154 (attach does
not exit when the container stops -- that is the hang, not the data loss) and
#9597 / #23757, which are interesting for a different reason: podman's own CLI
refuses attach against a non-running container, while the compat API endpoint
does not. That asymmetry went into the report.

Nothing to do here until upstream answers. If it is fixed, the require_running
guard in containers->attach (karr #53) can be revisited -- at minimum for the
Docker case, where it currently refuses a call that is harmless.
